Two alternative bases of use are proposed:

1. A free non-exclusive license solely for noncommercial use:
   LICENSE-NONCOMMERCIAL.md.
2. A separate paid commercial license entered into with the rightsholder:
   COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md is a draft of terms to fill in and agree.

Until the fields are filled in and the final documents are adopted by the
rightsholder, these drafts grant no rights of use. Availability of the
repository itself is not a grant of a commercial license. Statutory exceptions
to exclusive rights are not limited by this notice. Rights previously granted
separately are not changed by this draft.

This is not an open-source license. Release preparation: LICENSING.md.

English is proposed as the controlling text of the licenses, with Russian
informational translations under docs/ru/. That language priority must be
adopted by the rightsholder when the licenses are finalized; it is not in
force while the documents remain drafts.
